952\">Rossana De Simone\u003C/a>\u003C/p>  \u003Cp>ʾl\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"commentary\">\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>The first letter (Aleph) is written upright, and before writing the second letter (Lamed), the scribe rotated the vessel counterclockwise. It could be interpreted as an abbreviation (of a name) or a commercial sigla. The text appears to be complete.\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"bibliography\">\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Spagnoli 2012 53 fig.35 \u003C/li>\u003Cli> De Simone 2013 26 MO.5 fig.2 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002545\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002545\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"handnote\"> Line 1    Interlineation line 1 to 2    \u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"license\"> Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence. \u003C/div>",[188,191,194,197,200,202,205,208,211],{"id":189,"html":190},"editions","\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Jonathan Prag; edition source: \u003Ca href=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/EGNUE9CZ\">https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/EGNUE9CZ\u003C/a>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive-transliteration\" lang=\"xpu-Latn\">  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"xpu-Latn\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>ʾl \u003Cspan class=\"tei text-direction r-to-l\"> &nbsp;&nbsp;←\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Jonathan Prag; edition source: \u003Ca href=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/EGNUE9CZ\">https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/EGNUE9CZ\u003C/a>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-diplomatic-transliteration\" lang=\"xpu-Latn\">\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"xpu-Latn\